[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318031872","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3318031872","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3318031872,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FxSYA","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T10:14:51Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T10:14:51Z","body":"Alright, looks good to me now! Please [squash the commits together ](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/organization/pull_requests/creating_pull_requests.html#the-interactive-rebase) and it should be good to go.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318031872/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318432945","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3318432945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3318432945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fy0Sx","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T11:34:32Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T11:34:32Z","body":"@groud Note that this makes highlighting no longer affect:\r\n- scene tiles,\r\n- custom drawing (like `draw_circle` etc.) done on the TileMapLayer.\r\n\r\nFor custom drawing it would be enough to apply the highlighting to `TileMapLayer.self_modulate` as well (not just to quadrants' items).\r\nNo idea how to approach the scene tiles though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318432945/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318463422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3318463422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3318463422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fy7u-","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T11:41:40Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T11:41:40Z","body":"> scene tiles,\r\n\r\nAh that's a good point :thinking: . I probably did it that way for this reason. I don't think there's a way to solve that though, not sure if the current behavior is preferable to this new one then. I guess it could be discussed.\r\n\r\n> custom drawing (like draw_circle etc.) done on the TileMapLayer.\r\n\r\nI am not sure about this one. Self-modulate should impact those. \r\nBut anyway, if that's true, I think this one we can ignore, as using draw commands on a TileMapLayer is a very rare use case anyway.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3318463422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320573229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3320573229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3320573229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F6-0t","user":{"login":"Ir1ana","id":54417750,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NDE3NzUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54417750?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana","html_url":"https://github.com/Ir1ana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ir1ana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T18:03:39Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T18:03:39Z","body":"@kleonc @groud I optimized the code according to @kleonc comment and  added support for scene tiles, in a separate commit for easier diff reading.\r\n\r\nAs you can see, scene tiles highlight work, but there are some z-index issues which were already present before this PR. It can be fixed by setting the z-index in the editor.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"923\" height=\"543\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/00a86325-7810-44f3-ad96-9a9fd7e7ab3b\" />\r\n\r\nI also added `canvas_item_set_self_modulate` in an effort to add support for `draw_circle`, but it didn't work. I left it there anyway just in case. AFAIK, highlight on `draw_circle` does not seem to work in 4.5.\r\n\r\nHere my failing test on my branch:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"883\" height=\"480\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a194c67-de85-41b5-a55f-231e68511d1a\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320573229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323441014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3323441014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3323441014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GF692","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T10:40:18Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T10:40:18Z","body":"Alright, looks good to me now and does not have the drawbacks it had. I believe the two commits should be squashed together as they are both are needed to fix the initial issue, but aside from that, looks great.\r\nThanks again!\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323441014/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323851243","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3323851243","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3323851243,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GHfHr","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T12:41:25Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T12:41:25Z","body":"> I also added `canvas_item_set_self_modulate` in an effort to add support for `draw_circle`, but it didn't work. I left it there anyway just in case. AFAIK, highlight on `draw_circle` does not seem to work in 4.5.\r\n\r\nCustom drawing is affected by highlighting in 4.5 just fine (with the same nesting problem). In the current version of the PR it works as expected as far as I've tested.\r\n\r\n[nested-tilemap-layer-minimal-example_v2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22493237/nested-tilemap-layer-minimal-example_v2.zip) (`main.tscn`)\r\n\r\n- `v4.5.stable.official` [876b29033]\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fe71168-460c-4d2b-9f8b-8cba87787792\r\n\r\n- This PR (`v4.6.dev.gh-110768` [89a9be4e8])\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/09b1d0a4-749f-4b62-bb20-d5bd1912352b\r\n\r\n> Here my failing test on my branch:\r\n\r\nSo not sure why it didn't work for you.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> added support for scene tiles, in a separate commit for easier diff reading.\r\n> \r\n> As you can see, scene tiles highlight work\r\n\r\nApplying highlighting to scene tiles by modifying their roots' modulates like it's being done is not really reliable though, as user might modify scene root's modulate anyhow on their own, and such user-made changes won't trigger the internal update like `TileMapLayer::_scenes_update` where the highlighting would be reapplied. Meaning highlighting might be missing (depending on what changes user makes) between:\r\n- (after) user changing the modulate,\r\n- (before) subsequent internal update of the given cell containing scene tile.\r\n\r\nExample of the highlighting breaking:\r\n[nested-tilemap-layer-minimal-example_v2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22493237/nested-tilemap-layer-minimal-example_v2.zip) (`main_scenes.tscn`)\r\n\r\nScene tile is a plain Sprite2D with such script (changing modulate on a timer):\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends Sprite2D\r\n\r\nconst T := 2.0\r\nvar t := T\r\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\r\n\tt -= delta\r\n\tif t <= 0.0:\r\n\t\tt = T\r\n\t\tmodulate = Color(\r\n\t\t\trandf_range(0.5, 1.0),\r\n\t\t\trandf_range(0.5, 1.0),\r\n\t\t\trandf_range(0.5, 1.0),\r\n\t\t\t1.0\r\n\t\t)\r\n```\r\nIn action (`v4.6.dev.gh-110768` [89a9be4e8]):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98abfb4e-51cd-4ed6-89a4-64e5e718b081\r\n\r\nOf course it's a made up example specifically to show it breaking, but the user tweening the modulate etc. is rather not an unexpected use case. Maybe it being done in the editor / `@tool` script is less likely, but still. All I'm saying is that if we ship it like that, I expect it to be reported as a bug, sooner or later.\r\n\r\nFor the highlighting being applied to the scene roots' modulate to be reliable, we would need to somehow intercept calls / hook to `CanvasItem::set_modulate`. E.g. for TileMapLayer we intercept `CanvasItem::set_self_modulate` to handle the change properly by overriding `CanvasItem::set_self_modulate` (AFAIK it was made `virtual` specifically for that). But not sure how we could intercept `CanvasItem::set_modulate` for scene tile instances. Adding a signal like `modulate_changed` would be a trivial solution, but I suspect it would be not desired performance-wise. So, as already mentioned, I don't know how to tackle this properly.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3d91a48298f30c34747b9ad9a350be0bd66a87d4/scene/2d/tile_map_layer.cpp#L344\r\n\r\nNote this should also use the highlighted `layer_modulate` instead of `get_self_modulate()`. AFAICT a quadrant might be (re)created without any of the flags trigerring the render update being dirty (I think e.g. after placing a new tile).\r\n\r\n@Ir1ana And of course thanks for all the efforts! 🙂","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323851243/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323880893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3323880893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3323880893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GHmW9","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T12:50:01Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T12:50:01Z","body":"@kleonc We need to be realistic on that one, this is an editor-only feature, it's not a huge problem if it fails to update on that specific situation. Like any updates to the scene tiles, it's ok if they are not updated right away. That being said, I wonder if, when saved, a scene triggers the _changed signal in the TileSetSceneCollectionSource, and thus a redraw of the whole TileMapLayer. If not, that could be an improvement to implement eventually.\r\n\r\n> Note this should also use the highlighted layer_modulate instead of get_self_modulate(). AFAICT a quadrant might be (re)created without any of the flags trigerring the render update being dirty (I think e.g. after placing a new tile).\r\n\r\nRight, this should be updated too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323880893/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323972886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110768#issuecomment-3323972886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110768","id":3323972886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GH80W","user":{"lo